# Lives at the repo root because the build context (docker-compose.yml's
# `context: ../..`) is the repo root, not apps/backend - Docker only reads
# .dockerignore from the context directory.

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/coverage
**/.turbo

.git
.github
.claude
.vscode
.idea

**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

**/*.log
docs/
*.md
